# Item 5 of the 2026-10-14 Legion review (per-tick nav work): several simultaneous large orders. Four of the W3
# deadend probes stacked 100 cells apart on one map, each 120 bodies (12 per row, pitch 3 x 4, x 14-47) ordered in
# the same tick to its own dead end: A deadend-w2-n120-closed (2-cell corridor, closed), B deadend-w4-n120-closed,
# C deadend-w4-n120-room, D deadend-w6-n120-room (a 20x12 room at the end). The uplink lands the 480 orders over
# ticks 1-8, so the four formations are taken a few ticks apart and hand out their slots side by side.
# Keys: work.formation_ring_cells.max / work.slot_search_cells.max (the per-tick peak of the formation slot
# searches), work.legion_all.max, g.*.complete_n, g.*.arrived, g.*.done.
